learnings:
  - A 'param accepted but ignored' bug that's fixed in one copy almost always lives in the OTHER copies of duplicated logic. The University pack-loader exists in THREE places (MCP university-loader.ts, CLI core/university/storage.ts, serve server) — v6.6.4 fixed one, so the same bug resurfaced in the CLI and serve. ALWAYS grep for sibling implementations and fix/triage them together.
  - 'Package boundaries forced a port-not-extract decision: the CLI (packages/paradigm) can''t import the MCP loader (packages/paradigm-mcp), so the v6.6.4 contract was ported into storage.ts as additive packRoot params. The real consolidation (extract @a-company/university-core all three import) is filed as T-2026-06-01-001 — port-now-extract-later.'
  - 'The serve HTTP server was a DIFFERENT bug from the loader dup: it resolved the pack context in the CLI but never FORWARDED packRoot/packId to startServer, and the server hardcoded first-party detection. Test seam: extract buildPackConfig(options) as a pure exported function so ''serve --pack X mounts X'' is testable WITHOUT launching a server.'
  - serve --port was ignored due to commander declaring --port on BOTH the parent `university` command and the `serve` subcommand; fix is enablePositionalOptions() (program-global — verify sibling serve/watch commands still parse).
  - Onboarding partitioned by CATEGORY; sections-only packs (the v6.5 model) need section-aware partitioning gated on the RAW pack.yaml declaring sections (never manifest.sections.length, which is always populated post-normalize).
  - The university server is BUNDLED into the CLI dist by esbuild (dynamic import of @a-company/university/server, not externalized), so the serve fix ships with the @a-company/paradigm publish — no separate university publish strictly required.
